---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About MACH</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      MACH — the Machine-Actionable Catalog for Healthcare — is an open,
      evidence-based catalogue of open-source healthcare software, AI/ML models,
      datasets, standards, and data sources.
    </p>

    <h2>What makes it different</h2>
    <p>
      Most directories are lists. MACH judges every entry — <strong>Adopt</strong>,
      <strong>Assess</strong>, or <strong>Caution</strong> — and the judgement is a
      pure, deterministic function of measured signals: how actively a project is
      maintained, how widely it is adopted and used, and how it is licensed. No
      prose, no LLM: the same facts always produce the same verdict, and you can ask
      the catalogue to explain every rule that fired.
    </p>

    <h2>Verifiable lineage</h2>
    <p>
      Every harvested value — stars, downloads, licence, last commit — records the
      authoritative source it came from (GitHub, PyPI, Hugging Face). You can always
      answer "where did this number come from?" The hand-authored seed (name, URL,
      category) is the only human input; everything else is regenerated from sources.
    </p>

    <h2>Built for machines</h2>
    <p>
      MACH is served as a REST API and as a <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong>
      server, so AI agents can search and vet healthcare tools directly — using their
      own model, at no cost to the catalogue.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`{ "mcpServers": { "mach": { "url": "https://mach-render-deploy.onrender.com/mcp" } } }`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Tools exposed: <code>search_catalog</code>, <code>get_entry</code>,
      <code>list_entries</code>, and <code>explain_scoring</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Open</h2>
    <p>
      Code is Apache-2.0; the catalogue data is CC-BY-4.0. Entries are proposed via
      GitHub Issues and curated into the catalogue.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <a href="https://github.com/FORSE-H/MACH">github.com/FORSE-H/MACH</a> ·
      <a href="https://mach-render-deploy.onrender.com/docs">API docs</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .prose p { max-width: 42rem; }
    .prose h2 { margin-top: 32px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
